Office PDF (XTLaw)

This plugin includes portions of GenOffice by Mainfunc, Inc., licensed under the
Apache License 2.0, from revision 58dfd0b5b5eb3710efac0029b0452c61dba69035.
https://github.com/genspark-ai/genoffice

The GenOffice PDF editor is adapted to XTLaw's isolated plugin environment: the
code that runs in GenOffice's Electron main process (saving, text and image
editing, page operations) runs in the page instead, and the entries that need a
main process, an AI service or the system certificate store are not offered. The
adaptation is described in README.md and lexora-build/ of the XTLaw source
(apps/buddy/extensions/office-pdf).

Third-party components shipped in the package:

- PDF.js (Apache-2.0): rendering and text extraction. LICENSE-pdfjs.txt
- PDFium through @embedpdf/pdfium (BSD-3-Clause / Apache-2.0): editing of page
  content, run as WebAssembly. LICENSE-pdfium.txt
- HarfBuzz through harfbuzzjs (MIT): font subsetting, run as WebAssembly.
  LICENSE-harfbuzzjs.txt
- pdf-lib (MIT), fflate (MIT), React (MIT) and the other packages bundled into
  editor/; their licenses are carried in the bundle.
- Liberation fonts and the Noto Sans CJK SC subset (SIL Open Font License 1.1):
  editor/runtime/. LICENSE-OFL.txt

No source code from the happy-friday-lite application is included.
